[{:db/id "q-67703/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "121fb221-0a02-50ab-8f8b-671a0c28c0c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703/selection/89bbfcab2b786e6af03112df3094b429b69967ec226785add5cc488301d5ca26" :answer/id #uuid "1643c346-9326-5da5-9021-eb40088317ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "dd1c17d3-aa66-5374-954d-a0b6f827ea2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7416cd0f-45b3-541c-9bcf-4a8187e34e4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703/selection/2818e4c31c4efb328e8109219f816dc8f62d978373d20ea8fb8a4194e162a24f" :answer/id #uuid "3e13b19e-6447-5793-a9d7-811cbd1772e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5517b3de-1aa8-5abb-9744-83167954beb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-67703/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-67703/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" "q-67703/selection/89bbfcab2b786e6af03112df3094b429b69967ec226785add5cc488301d5ca26" "q-67703/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-67703/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-67703/selection/2818e4c31c4efb328e8109219f816dc8f62d978373d20ea8fb8a4194e162a24f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67703" :question/id #uuid "8c978569-5523-50ca-8c37-1ccfd41ba3f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-67703" :question/is-example false :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933898/assets/0b0074bb582011695cec9807beab1623c6aab894e0c6abeb1bf3068be6ed3543.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,3}f(x)=9.$ \n\nApplying the root rule, we get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}\\frac{\\sqrt{25-f(x)}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to \\,3}(25-f(x))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{25-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-67703/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10100e89-21d6-53c5-a7de-f14fd73ce4b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276812/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ef290df9-2242-528b-a664-cf7c14f3dfda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276812/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "546684cb-fc82-5ec8-97b7-93c2a7ca26eb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276812/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-276812/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276812" :question/id #uuid "1be43615-7dc6-54e4-af72-5f8d6df002b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-276812" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The multiplicity of the root $x=5$ in the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+5x+50$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Since $x=5$ is a root of $p(x),$ the factor theorem tells us that $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x).$\n\nBecause $(x-5)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-5)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-5)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $1$ | $-8$ | $5$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $5$ | $-15$ | $-50$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{p(x)}{x-5}={x}^{2}-3x-10,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\np(x)=(x-5)({x}^{2}-3x-10).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =(x-5)(x+2)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x-5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $(x-5)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276812/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3a53bf2-3144-5da3-8ee7-54d1e6c8fd7d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122083/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "4bc2d236-48a2-53b2-8871-f873f03741b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122083/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b2c4e520-8b00-51fd-b292-7d83ec8587a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122083/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "751d5ec7-b18d-55c1-89f3-66f11a9b81d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122083/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d6c14c16-7a63-51e6-92c5-62b52440ab17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}